From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:24:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(gatewayclient): service credential helpers for
 in-stack loopback calls

The gateway's per-start service credential (gateway.token) authenticates
the root service to the gateway's management API. Expose it for calls to
the other components' loopback listeners, so they can stop taking
loopback as an identity:

- ServiceAuthorization: the "Bearer <token>" header value
- ServiceAuthorizationMatches: constant-time check of a presented header
  (Bearer or bare), never matching an absent or empty credential
- ServiceRequestEditor: for oapi-codegen clients; adds the credential to
  requests to loopback IPs that carry no Authorization of their own

The file is read with the existing bounded, symlink-refusing reader at
every call, so a restarted gateway's new credential is picked up.
This package is kept identical across the component repositories.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pkg/gatewayclient/gatewayclient.go           |  61 ++++++++++-
 pkg/gatewayclient/service_credential_test.go | 102 +++++++++++++++++++
